.TH OSDOCTOR 1 "2026-05-30" "osdoctor 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
osdoctor \- Linux desktop health checks for Arch/Hyprland systems
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B osdoctor
.RI < COMMAND >
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B osdoctor
runs a set of read-only health checks against the host system, the
package manager, the systemd service state, and the desktop session, then
prints a grouped report. It is aimed at Arch Linux systems running Hyprland
and Omarchy-style configurations, but the system, service, and package checks
are useful on any systemd-based Arch install.
.PP
All checks are read-only: osdoctor never changes system state, and normal
scans do not require root.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B scan
Run every check group (System, Services, Packages, Desktop). This is the
default action when no command is given.
.TP
.B system
Run only the system checks (kernel, root disk space, /tmp, memory).
.TP
.B services
Run only the service checks (failed system and user units).
.TP
.B packages
Run only the package checks (pacman lock, log, orphans).
.TP
.B desktop
Run only the desktop checks (Wayland session, Hyprland socket, Hyprland bind
commands, Waybar scripts).
.TP
.B version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B help
Print usage information and exit.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit results as a JSON document instead of the human-readable report.
.TP
.B \-\-strict
Treat warnings as failures for the purpose of the exit code. The displayed
status labels are unchanged.
.TP
.B \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage information and exit.
.TP
.B \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH "CHECK STATUS LEVELS"
Each check reports one of:
.B OK
(healthy),
.B WARN
(worth attention),
.B FAIL
(a definite problem), or
.B SKIP
(not applicable in this environment).
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
.B 0
All checks passed (no warnings, no failures).
.TP
.B 1
One or more warnings, but no failures.
.TP
.B 2
One or more failures (or, under \fB\-\-strict\fR, one or more warnings).
.TP
.B 3
Invalid usage or an internal/tooling error.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_SESSION_TYPE
Inspected by the Wayland session check.
.TP
.B HYPRLAND_INSTANCE_SIGNATURE ", " XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
Used to locate the Hyprland IPC socket.
.TP
.B HOME
Used to locate Hyprland and Waybar configuration files.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
If set, disables colorized output. Color is also disabled automatically when
standard output is not a terminal.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/hypr/hyprland.conf
Parsed for \fBexec\fR bind commands.
.TP
.I ~/.config/waybar/config.jsonc ", " ~/.config/waybar/config
Parsed for referenced local script paths.
.TP
.I /var/lib/pacman/db.lck
Presence indicates a locked pacman database.
.TP
.I /var/log/pacman.log
Checked for existence and readability.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Run all checks:
.B osdoctor scan
.TP
Machine-readable output:
.B osdoctor scan \-\-json
.TP
Only the desktop checks, failing on warnings:
.B osdoctor desktop \-\-strict
